From: mtbl23 <182822903+mtbl23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:31:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Use the vanilla comparator signal when an inventory's max
 stack size was lowered

The cached Lithium signal strength assumes the default max stack size. Paper API can lower it per inventory, which changes
the signal, so those inventories use the vanilla calculation. Without this a comparator next to such a hopper evaluated a
different level and scheduled its update a tick off from Paper. Found with the differential hopper test (seed 31, tick 1509).

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/inventory/AbstractContainerMenu.java b/net/minecraft/world/inventory/AbstractContainerMenu.java
index 99fd3a3ba6a294556e9b843a3b479c2a6a1313e5..08557f97de8b32d62acfe2404f2cbca31f90cb5d 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/inventory/AbstractContainerMenu.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/inventory/AbstractContainerMenu.java
@@ -909,7 +909,8 @@ public abstract class AbstractContainerMenu {
 
         float totalPercent = 0.0F;
 
-        if (net.caffeinemc.mods.lithium.common.SleepingBlockEntityConfig.ENABLED && container instanceof net.caffeinemc.mods.lithium.api.inventory.LithiumInventory optimizedInventory) return net.caffeinemc.mods.lithium.common.hopper.InventoryHelper.getLithiumStackList(optimizedInventory).getSignalStrength(container); // Leaves - Lithium Sleeping Block Entity
+        // The cached strength assumes the default max stack size; Paper API can lower it per inventory, which changes the strength
+        if (net.caffeinemc.mods.lithium.common.SleepingBlockEntityConfig.ENABLED && container.getMaxStackSize() == Container.MAX_STACK && container instanceof net.caffeinemc.mods.lithium.api.inventory.LithiumInventory optimizedInventory) return net.caffeinemc.mods.lithium.common.hopper.InventoryHelper.getLithiumStackList(optimizedInventory).getSignalStrength(container); // Leaves - Lithium Sleeping Block Entity
         for (int i = 0; i < container.getContainerSize(); i++) {
             ItemStack itemStack = container.getItem(i);
             if (!itemStack.isEmpty()) {
